# CODEOWNERS — BlockHaven-Labs/esustellar
#
# Why this file exists (#1123)
# ---------------------------
# `CONTRIBUTING-INFRA.md` states "All infra changes must be reviewed — no direct
# pushes to main", and `docs/branch-protection.md` enforces "at least 1 approval"
# on `main`. That generic rule routes an infra PR to whoever reviews fastest,
# not to someone with infra context: a Terraform module change or a
# `NetworkPolicy` edit can be approved by a reviewer with no AWS/k8s
# experience and nothing in the merge process objects.
#
# The rules below make the required-reviewer set explicit for every path that
# changes running infrastructure.
#
# How to turn these rules into *enforced* review
# ------------------------------------------------
# CODEOWNERS on its own only requests a review. To make it mandatory, the
# `main` branch protection rule must list these owners under
# "Require review from Code Owners". Pair this file with that setting — see
# `docs/branch-protection.md`.
#
# On the owner team
# -----------------
# The org currently has no `infra-platform` team, so `@BlockHaven-Labs/infra-platform`
# below would be a silently-ignored no-op (GitHub cannot resolve an unknown team
# to a reviewer). Until that team is created, the active owners are the two
# accounts that hold write access to this repository. When the team is created:
#   1. add @BlockHaven-Labs/infra-platform to every block below, and
#   2. remove the individual-owner lines.
#
# Refs: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

